        "description": "Ask the gateway for the payment status of a VA (SNAP service code 26).\n\nThe pre-request script signs exactly like Inquiry and Payment do — see those for the mechanics.\n\n**What is different about this endpoint**\n\nBefore answering, the gateway verifies any NOT-yet-settled account against BCA's own Inquiry Status service and corrects its stored record when BCA knows better. So one call here can exercise the whole outbound path: B2B token acquisition, the signed call to BCA, and the reconciliation write.\n\n- A stored status of `00` is final — BCA is never consulted again.\n- Any other stored status (`01`, `02`, `03`) is re-verified on every request.\n- An account whose row has no `inquiryRequestId` cannot be reconciled at all: BCA generates that identifier, and a fabricated one matches nothing on their side.\n\n**The response never tells you whether BCA was reached.** A bank outage degrades to the stored answer on purpose, so a 200 is not evidence the bank answered. Read the server log instead:\n\n```\ndocker compose logs -f app | grep reconcile\n```\n\n| log event | meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `reconcile_applied` | the stored record was corrected |\n| `reconcile_failed` | BCA unreachable — answer came from storage |\n| `reconcile_unusable` | BCA answered with something unreadable |\n| `reconcile_skipped` | no stored inquiryRequestId, so BCA cannot be asked |\n| *(no line)* | stored status already `00` — final |\n\n**paymentFlagStatus**\n\n- `00` Success payment flag\n- `01` Reject payment flag by partner\n- `02` Timeout between switcher and partner. Counts as success when the company's reconciliation type is reversal or force settle — configured per vendor as `VENDOR_RECONCILIATION_TYPE`, in which case it is stored as `00`.\n- `03` Pending between BCA and the partner\n\n⚠️ Do NOT manually edit the Body tab — the pre-request script overwrites it."
      },
